## Context

The author installed and used v0.3.15/v0.3.16 live, right after ticket 0742's
persisted switch shipped, and reported nine distinct findings in one session
while actually clicking through the dialog. None of these were caught by the
Fable UX review or by any test — a review of prose and a test suite both miss
what only running the thing shows.

## Findings and fixes

1. **Jargon disclosures.** `launch-worker`/`launch-disable` used "shared
   worker", "native work", "thresholds", "what it consumes" — internal terms
   that read as noise to a user. Rewritten in plain language, tying back to
   the free-memory/free-disk figures the launch question already states.
2. **Active-file box flicker.** The box holding the current filename normally
   wraps to two lines; between one document settling and the next being
   admitted, the shorter "No indexing under way" message let it collapse to
   one line and back — a visible blink at every handoff. Fixed with a
   `min-height: 3em` reservation.
3. **Census-account table**: colon between label and count, no alignment, no
   separation from the readings above it. Rewritten as a genuine two-column
   table (`formatSDTColumns`): labels padded, numbers right-aligned to one
   shared column width, no punctuation, a blank line ahead of it.
4. **Zotero's own full-text stats printed as raw JSON** inside the
   `sdt-fulltext` disclosure. Reformatted through the same column table,
   reading whatever fields the real object carries (`humanizeSDTKey`) rather
   than naming them in advance — unverified on this host per ticket 0746.
5. **"Nothing is scanned" was false**: files scanned in earlier sessions, or
   earlier in the current one before switching off, are not undone by "off".
6. **"Nothing is sent for indexing" conflated two different things**: it read
   as if Zotero's own indexing also stopped, and said nothing about a job
   already in flight. Both switch-state-off findings fixed together: "No new
   attachment is checked while it stays off; one already under way still
   finishes. Zotero's own full-text indexing is unaffected."
7. **ESC did not close the dialog.** A bare `chrome,dialog=no` window carries
   none of a XUL `<dialog>`'s key bindings. Added a `keydown` listener that
   closes on Escape, through the same `dialog.close()` path `unload` already
   uses.
8. **The on/off button changed screen position when clicked**, because it sat
   right after a state description whose length changes drastically between
   "Indexing is on." and the (then much longer) off sentence. Fixed by
   pinning the button to the row's fixed right edge (`justify-content:
   space-between`) rather than reordering the button before the state text —
   the salient state should still lead in reading order.
9. **New: a separate "About and limitations" disclosure.** The version/
   compatibility line and the two consent-box disclosures used to live loose
   or bundled inside the debug/log disclosure (`sdt-tech-details`), which a
   reader opens to chase a *problem*, not to learn what the add-on does. Split
   into its own `sdt-about-details` disclosure, independent of the debug one.

## Also here (not a live finding, batched because touched by the same review)

Widened the host-API guard's search path (`tests/test_sitter_host_apis.py`,
ticket 0746 line of work) to include `~/.local/Zotero_linux-x86_64`, the
Zotero-provided Linux installer's own default target — this host's real
install sat there, distinct from the manual-tarball path already listed.

## Test

- `tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs`: switching off mid-census freezes the
  progress bar (already landed in PR #485, unaffected here); the census
  table has no colon, one shared right-aligned column, and a blank-line
  separator; the About disclosure holds the moved disclosures and the
  environment line; the switch row's `space-between` declaration and the
  active-file box's reserved height.
- `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs`: Escape closes the dialog (an unrelated
  key does not), verified red against the unfixed code.
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`: `census-total-label` replaces the removed
  `census-row`/`census-total` templates; the `document`-ban test now passes
  against the rewritten disclosures; two `_site` anchors updated to track
  code the refactor moved (one drifted into an unrelated function and caught
  a false positive on `(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`).

## Verification

- [x] All four `.mjs` suites pass
- [x] `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`, `tests/test_sitter_host_apis.py` pass, and
      the host-API guard now genuinely checks against this host's install
- [x] `make check-fast` — 1310 passed, 1 pre-existing environmental failure
      (podman rootless-container store, unrelated, documented this session)
- [x] Manifest/update.json bumped 0.3.16 -> 0.3.17, version guard clean

## Exit criteria

Every finding above has a corresponding code change and, where mechanically
checkable, a driven test.
